@startuml LogiShop_Sequence_ThesisStyle
!theme plain
skinparam Shadowing false
skinparam SequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #222222
  LifeLineBorderColor #222222
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantBorderColor #6B4E9B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8E0F5
      ' light purple header/footer feel (same style family as reference)
  ActorBorderColor #6B4E9B
  ActorBackgroundColor #E8E0F5
}

title Figure X.X. Sequence diagram — main interactions in LogiShop (logistics DSS)

actor "User" as U
participant "Frontend" as FE
participant "Backend" as BE
database "Database" as DB

== Connect and submit shipment request ==

U -> FE : Connect to home page
U -> FE : Navigate to create-shipment page
U -> FE : Enter shipment details (parties,\npackage, corridor / locations, …)

U -> FE : Submit shipment request
FE -> BE : Send shipment request (validated payload + auth token)

BE -> BE : Validate input and enforce\nrole = customer

BE -> DB : Insert new order (status pending review)
DB --> BE : Confirm saved

BE --> FE : Return confirmation + order identifier
FE --> U : Display “Request submitted —\nawaits staff review”

== Staff review and approval ==

note over U, FE
  **Operational user** (staff or administrator)\n— same Frontend / Backend / Database stack
end note

U -> FE : Open staff review queue
FE -> BE : Request pending shipment list
BE -> DB : Query orders awaiting approval
DB --> BE : Return pending rows
BE --> FE : Return list
FE --> U : Display review queue

U -> FE : Approve request / add or correct data\n(assign carrier tracking number, …)
FE -> BE : Send approval and shipment updates

BE -> BE : Verify staff or admin role

BE -> DB : Update order (approved, tracking #, notes, …)
DB --> BE : Return updated record

BE --> FE : Return updated order
FE --> U : Display approved shipment state

== Track visibility (refresh) ==

U -> FE : Open order detail / tracking view
U -> FE : Request latest carrier status (sync)

FE -> BE : Request refresh of order + tracking

BE -> BE : Authorize user for this order\n(scoped by role and approval rules)

BE -> DB : Fetch order and tracking number
DB --> BE : Return order row

opt tracking number is assigned
  BE -> BE : Call carrier tracking service\n(e.g. UPS) and normalize events
  BE -> DB : Store scan history / update delivery fields
  DB --> BE : Confirm persistence
end

BE --> FE : Return current order and tracking timeline
FE --> U : Display status, activities,\nand operations map (if used)

@enduml
